  "correction": {
    "scope": "One copy-only Swift fixture plus draft source/mutation/reference-model guards; no production source, reducer, navigation, counter, snapshot, fixture action, transport, or native control changes.",
    "gesture_policy": [
      "Observe and settle the exact known Home alias/list/overlay before deciding to move. Up/down come from finite bounded full-frame geometry, not a nil readiness value or a selector fallback.",
      "Use the same public list with .slow swipeUp or swipeDown. No coordinate, drag, alternate selector, direct application callback, navigation, or target activation retry.",
      "For an above-list target choose down; for a below-list target choose up. A contained overlay-overlapping card chooses the larger vertical free band only if the whole card fits. Horizontal overflow, oversized/nonfinite geometry, or no fitting band does not choose a direction.",
      "An initial not-yet-composed target permits bounded up-search only while exact identity has never been seen. After any sighting, disappearance resets sampling and cannot restart blind search. Ambiguous identities explicitly fail.",
      "Every decision needs six samples near the FIRST anchor (0.5point component tolerance), same direction and all measured frames; invalid/moved/changed-direction samples reset. Full-geometry-ready also reuses every existing strict readiness predicate and cross-checks recaptured frames."
    ],
    "bounds": {
      "gesture_maximum": 8,
      "decision_windows_maximum": 9,
      "samples_per_window_maximum": 24,
      "required_consecutive_samples": 6,
      "sampling_interval_seconds": 0.25,
      "diagnostic_rows_per_home_maximum": 216,
      "diagnostic_bytes_per_row_maximum": 2048,
      "final_single_activation_maximum": 1
    },
    "hittability": [
      "Existing l08HomeGeometry checks all original existence/enabled/full-card/overlay8point/environment predicates before target/list.isHittable; neither hit requirement is removed.",
      "Generic readiness predicate for Home dispatches through l08HomeGeometry rather than asking for an offscreen hit point first. Non-Home public controls retain their original predicate.",
      "Public diagnostic measures frame first and queries hittability only for a finite screen-contained frame. hittability_queried=false records NOT_QUERIED and omits hittable; it never fabricates false or claims readiness. This diagnostic is not the admission predicate."
    ],
    "remaining_guard_sequence": "All list gestures -> untouched/fresh zero observer -> original six first-anchor full-geometry samples -> immediate near target frame/enabled/hittable -> exactly one target.tap() -> fresh read-only exact one callback acknowledgement.",
    "limits": [
      "Slow velocity does not guarantee a pixel displacement or convergence. Persistent invalid geometry or oscillation still fails within bounds without activation.",
      "Samples remain non-atomic XCTest reads; stability and final cross-checks mitigate but cannot prove runtime delivery.",
      "No gesture occurs after the fresh-zero/final-geometry guard. No failure is caught or converted into readiness.",
      "The strict file-protection failure remains unchanged and is not excused by Simulator volume diagnostics."
    ]
